        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Determining the Loaded CG of a ",
            "font_name": "Arial,Bold",
            "font_size": 12.0,
            "color": "#EF4144",
            "is_bold": true,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              44.97305679321289,
              257.68927001953125,
              56.97305679321289
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Helicopter",
            "font_name": "Arial,Bold",
            "font_size": 12.0,
            "color": "#EF4144",
            "is_bold": true,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              56.97305679321289,
              130.3560028076172,
              68.97305297851562
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The empty weight and empty weight center of gravity ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              74.62269592285156,
              311.5110168457031,
              84.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "(EWCG) of a helicopter are determined in the same way ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              87.12269592285156,
              311.5200500488281,
              97.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "as for an airplane. See Chapter 5, Single-Engine Aircraft ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              99.62269592285156,
              311.6229553222656,
              109.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weight and Balance Computations. The weights recorded ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              112.12269592285156,
              311.50701904296875,
              122.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "on the scales supporting the helicopter are added and their ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              124.62269592285156,
              311.5250244140625,
              134.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "distances from the datum are used to compute the moments ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              137.12269592285156,
              311.5150146484375,
              147.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "at each weighing point. The total moment is divided by the ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              149.62269592285156,
              311.5040588378906,
              159.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "total weight to determine the location of the CG in inches ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              162.12269592285156,
              311.5030517578125,
              172.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "from the datum. The datum of some helicopters is located at ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              174.62269592285156,
              311.5030517578125,
              184.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "the center of the rotor mast, but since this causes some arms ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              187.12269592285156,
              311.4860534667969,
              197.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "to be positive (behind the datum) and others negative (ahead ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              199.62269592285156,
              311.5069885253906,
              209.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "of the datum), most modern helicopters have the datum ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              212.12269592285156,
              311.5699157714844,
              222.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "located ahead of the aircraft, as do most modern airplanes. ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              224.62269592285156,
              311.5059814453125,
              234.62269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When the datum is ahead of the aircraft, all longitudinal ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              237.12269592285156,
              311.5039978027344,
              247.12269592285156
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "arms are positive.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              249.62269592285156,
              142.82000732421875,
              259.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The lateral CG is determined in the same way as the ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              274.6226806640625,
              311.3929138183594,
              284.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "longitudinal CG, except the distances between the scales and ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              287.1226806640625,
              311.3500671386719,
              297.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "butt line zero (BL 0) are used as the arms. Arms to the right ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              299.6226806640625,
              311.50701904296875,
              309.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "of BL 0 are positive and those to the left are negative. The ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              312.1226806640625,
              311.5059814453125,
              322.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "butt line zero (or sometimes referred to as the buttock) is a ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              324.6226806640625,
              311.5050048828125,
              334.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "line through the symmetrical center of an aircraft from nose ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              337.1226806640625,
              311.50897216796875,
              347.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "to tail. It serves as the datum for measuring the arms used to ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              349.6226806640625,
              311.5070495605469,
              359.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "find the lateral CG. Lateral moments that cause the aircraft ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              362.1226806640625,
              311.51202392578125,
              372.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "to roll clockwise are positive (+), and those that cause it to ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              374.6226806640625,
              311.5020446777344,
              384.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "roll counterclockwise are negative (–).",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              387.1226806640625,
              226.12002563476562,
              397.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To determine whether or not a helicopter is within both ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              412.1226806640625,
              311.429931640625,
              422.1226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "longitudinal and lateral weight and balance limits, construct ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRoman",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              72.0,
              424.6226806640625,
              311.508056640625,
              434.6226806640625
            ]
          },
          {
